Pull Request resolved: https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/163144
Approved by: https://github.com/CaoE, https://github.com/mingfeima, https://github.com/jansel

Drop uncalled inlineable manual computation functions.

ShardMapExport pass runs before ExportNamedComputation pass on StableHLO export pipeline. ShardMapExport creates a new function for each manual computation, even they are within the named computations originated from the same function. ExportNamedComputation deduplicates named computations only based on input/output shardings, and as a result it ends up uncalled manual computations.

For example:

%0 = sdy.named_computation<"foo"> {
  %2 = sdy.manual_computation {} ...
}
%1 = sdy.named_computation<"foo"> {
  %2 = sdy.manual_computation {} ...
}

----> (ShardMapExport) ---->

%0 = sdy.named_computation<"foo"> {
  %2 = call @xla.sdy.inlinable_manual_computation_body
  ...
}
%1 = sdy.named_computation<"foo"> {
  %2 = call @xla.sdy.inlinable_manual_computation_body_0
  ...
}
...
func.func @xla.sdy.inlinable_manual_computation_body {...}
func.func @xla.sdy.inlinable_manual_computation_body_0 {...}

----> (ExportNamedComputations) ---->

%0 = call @foo
%1 = call @foo
...
func.func @xla.sdy.inlinable_manual_computation_body {...}
func.func @xla.sdy.inlinable_manual_computation_body_0 {...}
func.func @foo {
  %0 = call @xla.sdy.inlinable_manual_computation_body
  ...
}

